		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Mass Ratio Workaround?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2485#p2485"><![CDATA[
Here's another approach which could measure this "stress" more directly. The solver could simply measure the convergence of the velocity error. If the velocity error is not converging to zero fast enough, then the mass difference could be reduced for the next time step (or even the next iteration).<br><br>I'm guessing this would require a bit of tweaking to get a good benefit, but it should handle the different cases gracefully. In other words, we don't want to tweak the mass values when convergence is good.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=12">Erin Catto</a> — Fri Nov 17, 2006 7:13 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
