Hi,<br><br>The solver that I?m using to resolve collisions has the limitation that it does not converge well for large mass ratios. (I believe this is the case for most real-time solvers) but the game I?m working on calls for objects with vastly different weights. (E.g. think of a soldier being able to push a gigantic tank) <br><br>How do most solvers work around this issue? I can easily detect that one object should be heavier than the other and regard it as infinitely massive, but this opens up the door to objects being pushed through the ground. This seems like it?s an issue most games need to solve but I?ve never seen it mentioned.<br><br>Any ideas or tips would be greatly appreciated?<br><br>-Evan<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=65">Evan Christensen</a> — Mon Oct 30, 2006 11:52 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
